  "notes": [
    "May add authority (grants, writes, roles or secrets) in: sessions, ship. Auto-updates accept it; turn them off to review first.",
    "Skip the open backlog on a new repo, and Ship's add leaves code review off",
    "Add a repo with its own settings, and a cleaner Ship page",
    "Code mode: typed tool files and scripts in the box instead of the MCP tool list",
    "A PR comment people can read at a glance",
    "Post each finished turn's reply on the task",
    "Code review and ship read the change feed instead of polling GitHub",
    "A compact, readable repo settings panel",
    "Sessions page, terminal and phone UI",
    "Session agent and event watches",
    "Show each PR's risk tier on the one review comment",
    "Opencode engine for sessions",
    "Session job profile",
    "Release train batches deploys hourly (release_window_minutes, default 60)",
    "Judge each check name by its newest run at the head",
    "Adapt the open-PR page size per repo so big repos don't time out",
    "Stop blanking VAULT_FOLDERS and create the vault folders at setup",
    "A vault write root must be a searchable directory, and an unset vault must not fail the host check",
    "Name the Slack sign-in tile for what it gates",
    "Host setup changed (ops/setup.sh or ops/vm): an update runs apply only, so running the installer again may be needed (curl -fsSL https://get.aidenhq.ai | sh)."
  ],
